CampusShield database migrations (Alembic)

Operational instructions live in ../DATABASE_SETUP.md.
Schema design and rationale live in ../DATABASE.md.

    .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head      apply
    .venv/bin/alembic downgrade base    roll back everything
    ./scripts/test_migration.sh         full test from an empty database

Layout
    env.py                          URL resolution; Flask-Migrate compatible
    script.py.mako                  template for new revisions
    versions/0001_initial_schema.py  8 schemas, 24 enums, 34 tables, 1 view,
                                    18 trigger functions, 19 triggers

Two things to know before editing anything here:

1. Autogenerate is not used and target_metadata is None. The schema is
   hand-written DDL — cross-schema foreign keys, partial unique indexes,
   PL/pgSQL triggers, RLS, and CHECK constraints that SQLAlchemy cannot model.
   --autogenerate cannot see any of them and will propose dropping them.

2. Never edit an applied migration; add a new one. 0001 has run against a
   database somewhere, and changing it makes that database's recorded history
   a lie.

This directory is the same layout Flask-Migrate manages. When the backend
exists, `Migrate(app, db)` picks it up and `flask db upgrade` works with no
changes to any file here.
